# Null Summoner's threshold ability is a static ability, so its "as long as there are seven or more cards in your graveyard"
# is asked whenever the cast would begin (CR 604.1, 611.3a, 207.2c), not once. Bot1 exiles Bot2's Lightning Bolt and mills
# itself to twenty cards with Brain Freeze (as in the twin
# "...casts-the-exiled-card-only-once-it-has-threshold-with-mana-of-any-type", where the Bolt is then cast). On Bot2's turn
# Soul-Guide Lantern exiles Brain Freeze from Bot1's graveyard as it enters, then is sacrificed to exile Bot1's whole
# graveyard: with none there and Mox Pearl still open, the instant can't be cast from exile any more. It stays in exile.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Null Summoner
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Brain Freeze
Island x30

[Bot2 Deck]
Lightning Bolt
Soul-Guide Lantern
Mountain x20

